WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.950
this new book, The Infinite Game is exactly
the same. It's me on my journey which is

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.860
the same journey that we're all on.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.940
Which is I'm living in the world I'm

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.599
functioning in the world I'm an idealist
I talk about the world I want to live in

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:18.930
and quite frankly I got tired of people
in power, people who run companies,

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:24.990
people who work on Wall Street telling me then
I'm naive I'm stupid

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:30.090
and I don't understand how business works and when I
discovered this little book called

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:35.700
Finite and Infinite Games by James Carse that was written in 1986, it gave me

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.469
a whole new perspective on how the world
actually works that we are at all

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:46.140
moments of all days players in games
that have no finish lines.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.760
There's no such thing as winning friendship. There's
no such thing as winning in marriage if

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.770
you think you're going to be number one
in your marriage it's not gonna go well

00:00:54.770 --> 00:01:00.899
and there's definitely no such thing as
winning business and yet you listen to

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.700
so many leaders and they talk about
being number one, being the best,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.439
beating their competition. They have no idea how the world is actually working

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:13.049
they're playing with the wrong mindset
for the game that they're actually

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:17.670
playing and when you play with a finite
mindset in an infinite game you damage

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.810
trust, you damage cooperation, and you
hurt innovation and eventually the

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:27.270
organization struggles and goes into
decline. For me this little idea the

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.110
reason I wanted to write about it is
this is a world as flat moment all that

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.960
discomfort that so many of us have at
work and we're told by out by the powers

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.509
that be and those that work in
finance that we're the naive ones

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:46.890
yet we're still uncomfortable with the way
these things are going. This is the world

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:51.299
is flat moment as I said. It turns out
that they don't understand how business

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:57.060
works and we're on to something and I
wrote this book for two reasons

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.340
it wasn't to convince or convert anybody it
was a rallying cry to anyone who thinks

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.700
that the way that we're conducting
business these days the kind of form of

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.420
capitalism that we've built that there's
something wrong with it

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.420
I can't quite put my
finger on it but it feels uncomfortable

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:19.650
and it was also to show us what
finite mindedness looks like so we

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.280
can recognize finite minded companies
and finite minded leaders so we can

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.600
avoid working for them.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.620
This is like a little manifesto

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:34.860
of the world that could be and I hope
it's one more step to advancing to this

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:40.340
world in which we can wake up inspired
feel safe and return home fulfilled.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.090
I'm so grateful to all of you
who are in this business.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.237
We are compatriots in this movement and thank
you so so much

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.140
for helping me spread these ideas

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.060
because together we're
making a difference

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.320
we really are making a difference.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.940
Thank you very much

